module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.ComponentUniqueness.RankTwo.Parabolics.Models
public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.ComponentUniqueness.RankTwo.NonCharacteristicTwo.Definitions
public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.Preliminaries.NaturalAction

/-!+# Earlier action inputs for the larger-field paragraph

The ambient group here contains the original M and I. Relative normality
of L is supplied through `NonCharacteristicTwo.ComponentSetup I L M Yplus S`;
its local configuration lives in the actual I/C_I(L), not in the ambient
group modulo an absolute centralizer. That existing input also retains
I = LS, Y₊ ≤ L, the rank-two shadow and m₃(Y₊) = 2.

`ActionInputs` keeps the original natural orthogonal action on V and its
earlier plane geometry. The two Borel action facts are the permitted
earlier inputs to the paragraph. The residual is literally generated by
elements of order prime to six, rather than an iteration of O² and O³.
Neither a family reduction, a field-degree restriction, a centerless
cover nor a Borel-rank bound is a field of this structure.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), 15.3.2(1),
15.3.7, 15.3.10--11, 15.3.33, 15.3.36 and 15.3.41, and the larger-field
paragraph on printed p.1139. The O^π convention is GLS II, Chapter A, p.3.
-/

public section

open Subgroup
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.RankTwo.Parabolics.HigherField
variable {G : Type*} [Group G]

/-- Earlier action facts, expressed in the original ambient group so that
the natural action still belongs to all of M, not just M ∩ I. -/
structure ActionInputs (M Y S V V₁ V₂ Yplus B : Subgroup G) where
  natural : NaturalOrthogonalAction M V
  earlier : NonCharacteristicTwo.ActionSetup M Y S V V₁ V₂ Yplus
  noncentral : ¬ Yplus ≤ centralizer (V : Set G)
  borel_normalizes_moved : B ≤ normalizer ((⁅V, Yplus⁆ : Subgroup G) : Set G)
  residual_centralizes :
    closure {x : G | x ∈ B ∧ Nat.Coprime (orderOf x) 6} ≤ centralizer (V : Set G)

end CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.RankTwo.Parabolics.HigherField
